# Stitch UI design

Use Google Stitch via the project MCP server `stitch` (`.cursor/stitch-mcp-proxy.mjs`), not the OAuth-only `user-stitch` integration.

## Before generating or editing Stitch screens

1. Read `docs/agents/stitch.md` and `docs/design/alpine-air.DESIGN.md`.
2. Read `.stitch/metadata.json` for project ID, design system, and existing screens.
3. Always pass these defaults unless the user specifies otherwise:
   - `projectId`: `12447626312814512672`
   - `designSystem`: `assets/11762622741281556178`
   - `deviceType`: `DESKTOP`

## Porting Stitch → React

- Map to Alpine Air CSS variables in `src/index.css`; do not add parallel theme tokens.
- Preserve existing UX and information architecture ([ADR-0008](docs/adr/0008-ux-preservation-during-canonical-migration.md)).
- Follow feature-boundary rules in `AGENTS.md`.
- Run focused tests, typecheck, build, and browser smoke test after frontend changes.

## Generation patience

`generate_screen_from_text` and `generate_variants` are slow. Do not retry on timeout — poll with `get_screen` every ~30 seconds.
